2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2419) 'What happens when Git Bash rewrites your switches into paths? And when an empty title arrives as `\"\"` and `start` tries to run `\`?
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2419  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2419) 'Run your next slash-switch command from Git Bash under `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*'`.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2419  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2419) 'Git Bash on Windows runs slash-switch commands under a path-conversion guard
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2419  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2419) 'From Git Bash on Windows, a command with `/`-switches runs under `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*'`, so the switches are not rewritten into paths.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2419  1 LINE
 Text:Written

